   organisation are one You.
   "Control" means the power to direct management, by holding more than half of the voting power, by the
   right to appoint a majority of the directors or managers, or by contract. Control is tested on the day of
   use.
   "Affiliate" means any organisation that controls You, that You control, or that is under common control
   with You.
   "Regular contractor" means a natural person who was paid for work for You or for an Affiliate in at least
   four of the thirteen weeks before the day of use. Any paid work in a week counts for that week. Work in any
   role counts.
   "Worker" means a natural person who is an employee, owner, partner, member, or director of You or of an
   Affiliate and who works in that business, and a regular contractor of You or of an Affiliate.
   "Studio Size" means the number of distinct Workers on the day You use the Software. Each person is counted
   once. A part-time Worker counts as one person. Studio Size is the people of the business. It is not the
   number of people who open the Software.

2. Free use, for studios of 10 people or fewer. If Your Studio Size is 10 or fewer, the Licensor gives You
   a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to use, reproduce and adapt the Software for Your own use,
   including commercial work You are paid for by Your clients. It is non-transferable: You may not assign it.
   Giving copies to others is section 4 only.

3. Larger studios. If Your Studio Size is more than 10 on a day You use the Software, You have no licence under
   sections 2 and 4 for new use unless a commercial licence covers You. Studio Size is tested on each day of
   use. If it is 10 or fewer again, section 2 applies again from that day. If Studio Size goes above 10, You may
   finish a job already started, for 30 days after the first day it is above 10, and You may not start a new
   job in those 30 days. When the 30 days end, You stop using the Software unless You then have a commercial
   licence or Your Studio Size is 10 or fewer. Copies others already received under section 4 stay under this
   licence for those recipients. COMMERCIAL.md says how to ask. A commercial licence is a separate writing
   signed by the Licensor.

4. Sharing. If section 2 applies to You, You may give anyone a copy of the Software, changed or unchanged, at
   no charge. You include this licence, the NOTICE file, every copyright notice, every licence header and every
   project identifier, and You say which files You changed. The recipient receives that copy from the Licensor
   under this licence, and may use it only if the recipient's own Studio Size qualifies. That recipient's
   licence continues on its own terms if Yours ends. This section is the only right to distribute. It is not
   an assignment and it is not a sublicense.

